<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan money and bond markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Taiwan money and bond markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's money market and bond market are closed on Thursday due to a national holiday. They will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the overnight interbank rate ended at 5.267 percent against Tuesday's 5.445 close, with the 30-day commercial paper down to 5.15-5.20 against 5.50.</p>
<p>The bond market was quiet on Wednesday. -- Kevin Chen (5080815)</p>
</text>
